	5. Features
MVP (build first)
1. Accounts and approval: register, verify email, admin approves, role-based home screen.
2. Timetable: day and week views, venue and time, change and cancel flags, "Changed" badge.
3. Announcements: lecturers publish to a course, programme or campus; read status; in-app inbox.
4. Push notifications: new announcement, timetable change, deadline reminder.
Version 1.1 (after a month of pilot use)
5. Study materials: PDF upload, admin or lecturer approval, private download, saved offline.
6. Deadline calendar: assignments and academic events, reminders one day and one hour before.
7. Search and filters across announcements and materials.
Later (only if requested)
Swahili interface, student material submissions, assignment submission, lecturer office hours, exam timetable, campus map, web admin panel.
6. Offline and low-data design
Data cost is a real barrier, so this is a core requirement from day one.
* Every list loads from Room first, then syncs quietly in the background.
* Fetch only what changed (updated_at greater than last sync).
* Paginate everything. Never download a whole table.
* PDFs download only on tap, with file size shown and a "Wi-Fi only" option.
* Show last-synced time and a clear offline banner instead of errors.
* Clear the local cache and tokens on logout.
* Target: home screen usable offline within 2 seconds, app under 15 MB.
