14. Testing checklist
* ☐ RLS tests cover permitted and forbidden operations
* ☐ Pending accounts see no academic data
* ☐ Students cannot change role or status
* ☐ Lecturers cannot touch unassigned courses
* ☐ Draft and unapproved content hidden from students
* ☐ Timetable changes reach affected students only
* ☐ Times show correctly in East Africa Time
* ☐ App works offline after one sync
* ☐ Usable on a low-end phone with 2 GB RAM
* ☐ Cache and tokens cleared after logout
* ☐ Uploads enforce size, type and authorization
* ☐ Migrations and backups are versioned and recovery-tested
15. Pilot and success measures
Start with one programme, 30 to 60 students and 2 to 3 lecturers.
* Adoption: invited students who finish registration.
* Retention: weekly returning users after week 3.
* Reliability: timetable changes and announcements correct and on time.
* Usefulness: fewer missed announcements and deadlines (ask in a short survey).
* Lecturer effort: posting here is faster than WhatsApp.
* Performance: home screen loads fast on mobile data.
Success means students open it daily because it is the trusted source, not just that they registered.
16. Risks and how to handle themb
Risk
	Response
	Lecturers stop posting
	Make posting take under 30 seconds, get a department head to endorse it
	Competing with WhatsApp habit
	Be official and faster, offer optional "share to WhatsApp" later
	No access to official data
	Start with manual entry for one programme, pursue formal approval in parallel
	Privacy and records rules
	Synthetic data first, written approval before real student data
	Free-tier limits
	Monitor usage, compress PDFs, plan a paid tier and backups before wide launch
	Solo developer burnout
	Hold the MVP boundary, ship small, pilot early
	17. Costs
* Prototype and pilot: potentially TZS 0 on Supabase and Firebase free tiers (check current limits and pause policies).
* Google Play developer account: one-time fee, or distribute the APK directly during the pilot.
* Before wide launch: a paid database plan or reliable backups, and an optional domain.
* Avoid paid SMS and AI services until demand is proven.
